::PC_U02_L08_GP01::
Question ID: PC_U02_L08_GP01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.FA.1
Question:
If f(2) = 0 for a polynomial, which factor is supported?
{
=A. x - 2#Correct. A zero at 2 matches factor x - 2.
~B. x + 2#The zero is 2, not 0.
~C. x - 0#The zero is 2, not 0.
~D. x + 0#
}
::PC_U02_L08_GP02::
Question ID: PC_U02_L08_GP02
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.FA.5
Question:
Which value is excluded from f(x) = 9/(x + 3)?
{
~A. x = 3#This uses the wrong sign.
=B. x = -3#Correct. x + 3 = 0 when x = -3.
~C. x = 9#x = 0 gives denominator 3, so it is allowed.
~D. x = 0#
}
::PC_U02_L08_GP03::
Question ID: PC_U02_L08_GP03
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.EX.1
Question:
What does the 200 represent in P(t)=200(1.04^t)?
{
~A. Growth factor#The growth factor is 1.04.
~B. Decay factor#A base above 1 is growth, not decay.
=C. Initial value#Correct. The coefficient is the starting output at t = 0.
~D. Domain restriction#
}
::PC_U02_L08_GP04::
Question ID: PC_U02_L08_GP04
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.EX.2
Question:
What is the domain condition for log base 5 of x?
{
~A. x < 0#Negative arguments are not allowed.
~B. x = 0#0 is not allowed as a logarithm argument.
~C. all real numbers#Logarithms do not allow all real inputs.
=D. x > 0#Correct. A logarithm argument must be positive.
}
::PC_U02_L08_GP05::
Question ID: PC_U02_L08_GP05
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.FA.2; MLA.PC.FA.3
Question:
Which information helps determine a polynomial graph shape?
{
=A. Zeros, multiplicity, and end behavior#Correct. These are key polynomial graph features.
~B. Only graph color#The variable name does not determine shape.
~C. Only the variable name#A label alone does not determine graph behavior.
~D. Only the context label#
}